    "title": "Birders needed for Jan. 3 count",
    "text": "Birders who have a preference of where they want to explore during the 42nd annual winter bird count — the village, Beavertail peninsula, North End or farms — should contact Candy Powell ASAP at candacepowell48@gmail.com or 401-524-0562.\nThe annual event to tally the local avian population is Saturday, Jan. 3. Birders should rendezvous at 7 a.m. at the police station, 250 Conanicus Ave. Birders, who will then be divided into four groups to scour the island, should bring binoculars and appropriate clothing, including sturdy shoes.\nThe groups will meet at noon to report the sightings. The count, however, continues all day, so if there are areas not covered, or expected birds not seen, sightings in the afternoon and evening can still be reported to Powell.\nBirders unable to attend can observe birds from their yards. These people, however, should be specific to their location so they do not duplicate the groups’ sightings.",
